Follow-up to #3. briefing resolves a plugin:skill (and bare names that fall through to plugins) from installed_plugins.json, but never consults enabledPlugins. A plugin that is installed yet disabled via `"enabledPlugins": {"<plugin>@<marketplace>": false}` in settings.json is therefore still briefed, even though Claude Code itself does NOT load its skills or offer them to the model.

This is exactly the divergence the plugin exists to avoid: briefing injects a skill the harness would not, so an agent gets context that "cannot be there". A declaration pointing at a deliberately disabled plugin should fail (unknown skill), matching Claude Code.

resolve_plugin_skill/claude_plugins (hooks/briefing-preload) iterate the installed_plugins.json entries and stop there. They must skip any plugin whose merged enabledPlugins value is false.

Fix: read enabledPlugins from Claude Code's settings files with their real precedence (managed > project.local > project > user, verify against Claude Code behavior), key `<plugin>@<marketplace>`, and drop plugins set to false. Confirm the default for an installed-but-unlisted plugin (expected: enabled) so we do not regress plugins that were installed before the setting was written. Add tests: disabled plugin -> unknown; per-scope override (project re-enables a user-disabled plugin, and vice versa); unlisted plugin still resolves.

Out of scope of #3, noted in CLAUDE.md as a known gap.
